{
  "_readme": [
    "Source of truth for which Heroicons ship in rm/js/icons.js.",
    "Run `node scripts/gen-icons.mjs` after editing. `--check` fails if the",
    "generated file is stale; release_push.py runs it as a gate.",
    "",
    "`emoji` is the glyph this icon replaced. It is NOT decoration: icons.js",
    "keeps the reverse map so ICON.mode='emoji' (or labConfig.iconMode) can",
    "render the original glyph again with no deploy. That kill switch is the",
    "only rollback that reaches phones already on a TestFlight build.",
    "",
    "`solid: true` also emits the filled weight. Only mark it where an active",
    "or selected state actually needs one - every solid entry is ~600 bytes",
    "shipped to a phone.",
    "",
    "Counts are live-code occurrences in rm/js/*.js measured 2026-08-15.",
    "",
    "V3.861: `lucide: true` sources the icon from vendor/lucide/24 (Lucide, ISC) — the gap",
    "icons Heroicons does not ship (lab, bio, nature). Same 24-grid outline style; CSS owns the",
    "stroke width, so both libraries render at the same weight. `tint{}` maps coloured-shape",
    "emoji to a shape + colour."
  ],
  "heroicons": "2.2.0",
  "fallback": "question-mark-circle",
